Let $f(n)$ be the number of times you have to hit the $\sqrt{ }$ key on a calculator to get a number less than 2 starting from $n$. For instance, $f(2)=1, f(5)=2$. Let $\theta = 1021^\circ$, and let $n$ be an integer such that $-90 \le n \le 90$ and $\sin n^\circ = \sin \theta^\circ$. Define a function $g(n)$ as follows:  
$$
g(n) = 
\begin{cases}
f(n), & \text{if } n \text{ is even} \\
f(n) + 1, & \text{if } n \text{ is odd}
\end{cases}
$$
For how many integers $n$ in the range $-90 \le n \le 90$ is $g(n)$ odd?

